5. Unified Viability Conditions

We formulate conditions on the continuous evolution and on the discrete switches that together guarantee invariance of the safe envelope.

Consider an interval [\tau_k, \tau_{k+1}) with active graph A. The joint process (x_t,\theta_t) evolves according to (1) with graph A and (8). Its infinitesimal generator \mathcal{A}^{\mathrm{tot}}_A acts on smooth functions \phi(x,\theta) by

\mathcal{A}^{\mathrm{tot}}_A \phi = \mathcal{A}_A \phi + \mathcal{A}^\theta \phi.

Between interventions, the dynamics of L_t are

\mathrm{d}L_t = \big[ \mathcal{A}_A (\ln h(\cdot,A)) + \mathcal{A}^\theta (\ln V) \big] \mathrm{d}t + \mathrm{d}M_t,

where M_t is a local martingale comprising continuous and jump parts.

Condition 5.1 (Continuous viability). There exists a class‑\mathcal{K} function \alpha such that for every state (x,\theta) with active graph A and L > \ln\mathcal{V}_{\min},

\mathcal{A}_A (\ln h(\cdot,A)) + \mathcal{A}^\theta (\ln V) \ge -\alpha(L - \ln\mathcal{V}_{\min}). \tag{13}

Condition 5.2 (Impulse viability). At any intervention time \tau with pre‑intervention state (x,\theta) and graph A_{\mathrm{old}}, the selected action u \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(x) and new graph A_{\mathrm{new}} = \mathrm{do}(u)[A_{\mathrm{old}}] satisfy

\ln h(x, A_{\mathrm{new}}) - \ln h(x, A_{\mathrm{old}}) - C(u) \ge \ln\mathcal{V}_{\min} - L_{\tau-}. \tag{14}

These conditions ensure that the drift of L_t becomes non‑negative as the boundary is approached, and that jumps do not breach the envelope.

